From 1d967e7ff3da048cdaafb52ff90f1008e08b8385 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emaki contributors <emaki@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: find theme icons installed after startup

Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Yakymenko
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-only

Qt's icon loader reads each theme's directories once, so the icon of a
program installed while the shell runs stayed missing in
Quickshell.iconPath(name, true) until the shell restarted. On a miss, load
the themes again at most every two seconds and look once more. Qt also
keeps only the icon directories that existed at startup, so the reload adds
the data directories' icon directories that exist now (the first flatpak
install creates its export directory).

A missed name is looked up again when the two-second window ends and keeps
being looked up until two seconds after its miss (a package's icons can land
just after its desktop entry): one timer serves every miss, and
Quickshell.iconThemeRevision changes when one of them is found, so a
binding that reads it shows an icon installed after its first lookup.
Names still missing then are dropped until their next lookup, not retried
in a loop.
